context:
DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/allow_policies/{policy_id}
Removes an allow policy. After deletion, emails matching this pattern will be subject to normal security scanning and disposition actions.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; policy_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/block_senders/{pattern_id}
Removes a blocked sender pattern. After deletion, emails from this sender will no longer be automatically blocked based on this rule.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; pattern_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/investigate/bulk/{job_id}
Deletes the job, removing it from all list and detail endpoints. Only jobs in a terminal state (`COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED`, `FAILED`, or `SKIPPED`) can be deleted. To stop an in-progress job without removing it, use the cancel endpoint instead.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; job_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/content_policies/{policy_id}
Removes a content policy. After deletion, emails will no longer be evaluated against this pattern.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; policy_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/domains/{domain_id}
Removes email security protection from a domain. After deletion, emails for this domain will no longer be processed by Email Security. This action cannot be undone.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; domain_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/impersonation_registry/{impersonation_registry_id}
Removes an entry from the impersonation registry. After deletion, this identity will no longer be protected from impersonation.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; impersonation_registry_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/sending_domain_restrictions/{sending_domain_restriction_id}
Removes a sending domain restriction. After deletion, TLS will no longer be enforced for emails from this domain.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; sending_domain_restriction_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/trusted_domains/{trusted_domain_id}
Removes a trusted domain pattern. After deletion, emails from this domain will be subject to normal recent domain and similarity checks.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; trusted_domain_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/url_ignore_patterns/{pattern_id}
Removes a URL rewrite ignore pattern. After deletion, URLs matching this pattern will be rewritten again.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; pattern_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/allow_policies/{policy_id}
Retrieves details for a specific allow policy including its pattern, dispositions that are exempted, and whether it applies to all detections.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; policy_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/block_senders/{pattern_id}
Retrieves details for a specific blocked sender pattern including its pattern type, value, and metadata.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; pattern_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/investigate/bulk/{job_id}
Returns the status and details of a specific bulk action job.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; job_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/content_policies/{policy_id}
Retrieves details for a specific content policy including its pattern, targets, and metadata.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; policy_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/domains/{domain_id}
Retrieves detailed information for a specific protected email domain including its delivery configuration, SPF/DMARC status, and authorization state.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; domain_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/impersonation_registry/{impersonation_registry_id}
Retrieves details for a specific impersonation registry entry including the protected identity, email pattern, and synchronization source if directory-synced.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; impersonation_registry_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/sending_domain_restrictions/{sending_domain_restriction_id}
Retrieves details for a specific sending domain restriction including the domain requiring TLS and any excluded subdomains exempt from the TLS requirement.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; sending_domain_restriction_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/trusted_domains/{trusted_domain_id}
Retrieves details for a specific trusted domain pattern including its pattern value, whether it uses regex matching, and which detection types it affects.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; trusted_domain_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/url_ignore_patterns/{pattern_id}
Returns a single URL rewrite ignore pattern by its identifier.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; pattern_id (path)

PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/allow_policies/{policy_id}
Replaces an existing allow policy in full. Unlike PATCH, every field is taken from the request body, so optional fields that are omitted are reset rather than left untouched. Use this when managing policies declaratively.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; policy_id (path); body (body)

PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/block_senders/{pattern_id}
Replaces an existing blocked sender pattern in full. Unlike PATCH, every field is taken from the request body, so optional fields that are omitted are reset rather than left untouched. Use this when managing blocked senders declaratively.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; pattern_id (path); body (body)

PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/domains/{domain_id}
Replaces all mutable fields of a protected email domain in a single atomic operation. Unlike PATCH, all non-computed fields are required.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; domain_id (path); body (body)

PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/trusted_domains/{trusted_domain_id}
Replaces an existing trusted domain in full. Unlike PATCH, every field is taken from the request body, so optional fields that are omitted are reset rather than left untouched. Use this when managing trusted domains declaratively.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; trusted_domain_id (path); body (body)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/allow_policies/{policy_id}
Updates an existing allow policy. Only provided fields will be modified. Changes take effect for new emails matching the pattern.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; policy_id (path); body (body)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/block_senders/{pattern_id}
Updates an existing blocked sender pattern. Only provided fields will be modified. The pattern will continue blocking emails until deleted.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; pattern_id (path); body (body)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/content_policies/{policy_id}
Updates an existing content policy. Only provided fields will be modified.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; policy_id (path); body (body)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/domains/{domain_id}
Updates configuration for a protected email domain. Only provided fields will be modified. Changes affect delivery mode, security settings, and regional processing.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; domain_id (path); body (body)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/impersonation_registry/{impersonation_registry_id}
Updates an existing impersonation registry entry. Only provided fields will be modified. Directory-synced entries can't be updated.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; impersonation_registry_id (path); body (body)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/sending_domain_restrictions/{sending_domain_restriction_id}
Updates an existing sending domain restriction. Only provided fields will be modified. Changes affect which domains require TLS and which subdomains are excluded.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; sending_domain_restriction_id (path); body (body)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/trusted_domains/{trusted_domain_id}
Updates an existing trusted domain pattern. Only provided fields will be modified. Changes take effect for new emails matching the pattern.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; trusted_domain_id (path); body (body)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/email-security/settings/url_ignore_patterns/{pattern_id}
Updates an existing URL rewrite ignore pattern. Only provided fields will be modified.
Required: account_id (path) — Account identifier tag.; pattern_id (path); body (body)
